and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The First Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the First Conditional to talk about real possibilities in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will do   something. In that condition, something else will happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If you do some research,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> you'll find out this didn't happen until the 20th century. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If you have heard of Neil Armstrong, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> you may know that he was the first person to walk on the moon.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "If you google the Space Race, you can read how the U.S. and the Soviet Union took turns sending satellites and men into orbit. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you log onto the NASA website, you will see pictures and data sent back by dozens of space probes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If technology permits, there is no doubt that manned space exploration will one day take us to Jupiter, past the boundaries of our solar system, or even beyond.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modal Verbs in the Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs.  They come before the dictionary form (infinitive without <span class=\"italic\">to</span>) of the main verb. <br/>Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or obligation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use modal verbs in the passive voice. <br/>You use the passive voice when you want to focus on the \"receiver\" of the action, rather than the \"doer\" of the action. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The invention of the telescope was required before the stars and planets could be seen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Astronomy could only then be developed into a modern science.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Men began to wonder whether the stars and planets they saw could be explored.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The whole world waited to see who the race would be won by.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The Earth's strong gravitational pull would have to be overcome before rockets could escape the stratosphere.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Even more information could be sent back by those still travelling.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Here is the structure of a passive sentence:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + To be + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can add a modal verb before the To be:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + modal + To be + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<span class=\"italic\"> <ul><li> Astronomy <span class=\"strong\">could</span> only then  <span class=\"strong\">be developed</span> into a modern science.</li><li> The whole world waited to see who the race <span class=\"strong\">would be won by</span>.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "telescope ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a piece of equipment shaped like a tube that you look through to make objects that are far away appear larger and nearer", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  The invention of the telescope was required before the stars and planets could be seen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about the stars.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "astronomy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the science which studies the universe beyond the Earth's atmosphere", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Astronomy was developed into a modern science after the invention of the telescope.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "heavens", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the space that surrounds the Earth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  With their eyes on the heavens, men began to wonder whether the stars and planets they saw could be explored.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stratosphere", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the layer of the Earth's atmosphere between about 6 and 30 miles above the surface of the Earth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Earth's strong gravitational pull would have to be overcome before rockets could escape the stratosphere.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gravitational", "type": "name"}, {"content": "connected or pulled together by a strong force", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Earth's strong gravitational pull would have to be overcome before rockets could escape the stratosphere.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "satellite", "type": "name"}, {"content": " an object that revolves around a planet ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are satellites in space that revolve around our planet.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to orbit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to follow a circular path around another object like a sun or a planet", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The US and the Soviet Union took turns sending satellites and men into orbit. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "NASA", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an agency of the USA whose acronym means  National Aeronautics and Space Administration", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you log onto the NASA website, you will see pictures and data sent back by dozens of space probes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "probe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an object that explores the solar system and transmits data back to Earth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Space probes send pictures and data from space back to Earth.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob10aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "solar", "type": "name"}, {"content": "related to the sun", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"conte